      "token": "\"Let $G$ be a finite abelian group of order $n$. Let $x=(x_1,\\\\ldots,x_n)\\\\in G^n$ and let $w=(w_1,\\\\ldots,w_k)\\\\in\\\\mathbb{Z}^k$. Assume that\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\max_{a\\\\in G}|x^{-1}(a)|\\\\leq k.\\n$$\\n\\n**Weighted zero-sum conjecture.** There are a nonempty subset $I\\\\subset [1,k]$ and an injection $f:I\\\\mapsto [1,n]$ such that\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\sum_{i\\\\in I}w_i x_{f(i)}=0.\\n$$\\n\\nThis conjecture is suggested by the preceding weighted generalization of the standard zero-sum lemma, and would extend the unweighted case related to Gao's $n+D-1$ theorem. The source does not provide a resolution status.\"",
      "token_sha256": "2b4bcfad547a52d27d8826315ab388e4f57bf53a9db6d3ff3a648c245a7e9aa8",
      "decoded": "Let $G$ be a finite abelian group of order $n$. Let $x=(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)\\in G^n$ and let $w=(w_1,\\ldots,w_k)\\in\\mathbb{Z}^k$. Assume that\n\n$$\n\\max_{a\\in G}|x^{-1}(a)|\\leq k.\n$$\n\n**Weighted zero-sum conjecture.** There are a nonempty subset $I\\subset [1,k]$ and an injection $f:I\\mapsto [1,n]$ such that\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i\\in I}w_i x_{f(i)}=0.\n$$\n\nThis conjecture is suggested by the preceding weighted generalization of the standard zero-sum lemma, and would extend the unweighted case related to Gao's $n+D-1$ theorem. The source does not provide a resolution status.",
